statement:
Use the quasicategories, coherent functors, mapping spaces and universes of [def-cbc-enhanced-diagrams-cones] and [def-coef-complete-algebroid], the presentably monoidal convention of [def-coef-complete-algebroid], and the monoidal infinity categories, cocartesian edges and strong monoidal functors of [def-coef-monoidal-infinity-category]. Let $C$ be a small monoidal infinity category with structure map $C^\otimes	o N(\Delta^{\mathrm{op}})$, let $\mathcal S$ be the infinity category of small spaces, put $P(C)=\operatorname{Fun}(C^{\mathrm{op}},\mathcal S)$, and let $j:C	o P(C)$, $j(c)=\operatorname{Map}_C(-,c)$, be the Yoneda functor. Let $Q_C	o N(\Delta^{\mathrm{op}})$ be the right-fibration Day convolution of [lem-coef-day-relative-exponential-model], that is, the infinity-categorical pullback of $p^	imes:\operatorname{RFib}^	imes	o\operatorname{Cat}_{\mathcal U}^	imes$ along the coherent classifying algebra $\underline C$ of $C^\otimes$; it is a monoidal infinity category with fibre $P(C)^r$ over $[r]$, whose $r$-ary operation $\star_r$ sends $(F_1,\ldots,F_r)$ to the left Kan extension of $(c_i)\mapsto\prod_iF_i(c_i)$ along the opposite of the $r$-fold tensor functor $C^r	o C$ (for $r=0$, of the point along the unit $*	o C$). Then:

(1) for every $r\geq0$ the operation $\star_r:P(C)^r	o P(C)$ preserves small colimits separately in each variable; hence $P(C)$ with the monoidal structure $Q_C$ is presentably monoidal;

(2) the Yoneda functor has a strong monoidal enhancement $j^\otimes:C^\otimes	o Q_C$: a coherent functor over $N(\Delta^{\mathrm{op}})$ carrying every cocartesian edge of $C^\otimes$ to a cocartesian edge of $Q_C$, whose functor on fibres over $[r]$ is $j^r:C^r	o P(C)^r$ under the Segal identifications. In particular it supplies coherent equivalences $j(c_1)\star\cdots\star j(c_r)\simeq j(c_1\otimes\cdots\otimes c_r)$ for every $r\geq0$, including $\mathbf 1_{Q_C}\simeq j(\mathbf 1_C)$ for $r=0$. In the planar normal form of [lem-coef-monoidal-block-projection-coherence] for $C^\otimes$ and $Q_C$, with reduced operations $c_r$ and $\star_r$, these equivalences $\star_rj^r\simeq jc_r$ come with all tree-indexed compatibility simplices for substitution, grafting and unary identities, so that they form a morphism of unital planar operation systems;

(3) $j^\otimes$ is fully faithful: it induces equivalences on all mapping spaces of the total infinity categories over every base arrow.
